# An allowlist: the build context is only what the build stage reads, so
# nothing else — node_modules, dist, .git, tests and their fixtures, docs —
# can reach the image, whatever is added to the repository later.
*
!package.json
!package-lock.json
!.npmrc
!tsconfig.json
!tsconfig.build.json
!README.md
!LICENSE
!src

# Re-excluded after the allowlist, because a later rule wins: a local MCP host
# configuration holds real instance URLs and API keys, and an environment file
# may hold anything. Neither may enter the context, wherever one is placed.
**/.mcp.json
**/.env
**/.env.*
